+
+
+## Central adjudication
+
+One normalisation pass over all 185 tranche-and-anchor records after the tranches, which the
+tranches cannot do for themselves: a cross-record citation only coheres if both
+grades are adjudicated together, and tranche-local drift is invisible from
+inside a tranche.
+
+### Coverage
+
+185 records covered of 186 present: 13 adjudicated as anchors up front, 165
+further flat records and 7 per-area records across eight tranches.
+
+**The one record with no tranche row is ADR-239, this change's own doctrine
+record**, and completion review caught the artifact claiming full coverage while
+it was absent. It could not have had a row: it did not exist when the tranches
+were assigned. Its disposition is stated here instead, and the self-grading is
+visible rather than buried — `provenance: mixed`, `evidence: E3` by
+triangulation, `KEEP` pending the owner ruling its `status: proposed` waits on.
+One tranche reviewer graded it independently at E3, which is a single outside
+concurrence and nowhere near the sample `claim:adr-grade-accuracy-vs-gold`
+needs.
+
+No record was skipped and none was sampled — the owner's instruction was to
+question all of them, and the count is the check on that, which is exactly why
+the off-by-one mattered enough to write down.
+
+### Blinded overlap — the disagreement, published rather than smoothed
+
+17 records were assigned to a second reviewer who was not told it was a double.
+**16 came back doubled** (one reviewer covered its primary list only, so that
+record has a single grade — stated because a 17/17 claim would be false).
+
+Of the 16: **provenance agreed on 14, strength agreed on 14.** Three records
+disagreed, one of them on both axes. Adjudicated here, with the reasoning, so
+the resolution is auditable rather than asserted:
+
+| Record | Reviewer A | Reviewer B | Adjudicated | Why |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| ADR-009 | `mixed` / E1 | `human` / E0 | **`unknown` / E0** | The record carries no decision-maker marker at all — no council attribution, no "maintainer", no measurement. Both reviewers guessed, in opposite directions. `unknown` is what the file supports, and the contract's own rule forbids inferring `human` from absence. |
+| ADR-037 | E1 | E2 | **`agentic` / E1** | `:23` names the AI council as decider and `:69` records its unanimity — and unanimity is not evidence. The only anchor is an existing decoupled architecture (`:109`), which is one local observation. E2 needs a repeated or comparative measurement and there is none. |
+| ADR-085 | `mixed` | `human` | **`mixed`** | `:25` "explicit maintainer decision (the demand trigger)" and `:56-58` the verbatim owner instruction, with a two-round peer-reviewed council session choosing the mechanism. Human premise, agent mechanism — the textbook `mixed` case. |
+
+**What this measures, and what it does not.** 14/16 on each axis is an
+inter-reviewer agreement rate. It is **not** accuracy: reviewers who searched the
+same way against the same rubric can agree and both be wrong, and this
+repository has the receipt — 44 engine-shaped REJECTs accumulated under
+correlated council agreement and were disposed of by one measurement. So this
+number goes to `claim:adr-grade-accuracy-vs-gold` as an input, not as a result;
+that claim needs an externally adjudicated gold sample and stays `unbacked`.
+
+One datum points the same way. The anchor set itself carried a wrong provenance
+on ADR-104 for the duration of the sweep, adjudicated by the party that wrote
+the schema, and an outside pass caught it. That is one error in 13 anchors, which
+is not a rate — but it is a measured instance of the failure mode this design's
+independence limit predicts.
+
+### The heuristic's blind spot, measured
+
+`evidence_census.ts` proposed **E4 = 0** across all 186 records, and declared in
+its own header why: a heuristic cannot establish that a real consumer depends on
+an interface or that a legal obligation applies, so it never proposes E4.
+
+Reviewers found **3**. The clearest is ADR-205, whose basis is a court ruling on
+hotlink IP transmission — an external legal constraint applied to the decision it
+supports, which is the definition of E4 and is invisible to any marker scan.
+
+That is the census working as documented rather than failing: a stated blind
+spot, now measured at 3 records instead of asserted. It is also the concrete
+argument for keeping the census proposal-only — a pass that wrote its own
+grades would have written `E0`/`E1` over three E4 records and nobody would have
+looked again.
+
+### Cross-tranche convergence — where two reviewers found one class independently
+
+These matter more than any single row, because independent arrival is the
+closest thing this sweep has to corroboration.
+
+1. **Command-depth prohibition versus shipped tree.** Tranche 1 found ADR-044
+   banning colon namespacing while `dist/agent-src/commands/` ships 132
+   depth-2 and 8 depth-3 files; tranche 5 found ADR-003's "No sub-sub-commands.
+   Option B is rejected" breached by the same 8 commands, its locking contract
+   self-contradicting in one file, and `check_cluster_patterns.ts:30-32`
+   carving the shape out **by name** so CI cannot see it. Two records, one
+   breach, and a gate blinded by an allowlist.
+2. **`.py` citation rot is a corpus class, not a per-record slip.** Tranche 7:
+   12 of 25 records cite 27 distinct `.py` paths against a tree holding 2, both
+   eval fixtures. Tranche 8: ~7 more. Every anchor has a live TS equivalent, so
+   this is citation rot rather than capability loss — one batch AMEND, not
+   thirty judgements.
+3. **Supersession reciprocity has no check and the corpus has broken links.**
+   Tranche 2 counted 4 one-sided `supersedes`/`superseded_by` pairs and found
+   `check_adr_frontmatter.ts:470-476` admitting the gap in its own docstring
+   while fixing only `amends`. Tranche 5 hit the same class from the other side
+   (ADR-043 declares `supersedes: ADR-017`; ADR-017 still reads `accepted`,
+   `superseded_by: —`).
+
